---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { products, site } from "../../data.mjs";
const sizeChartModels = ['KP01-V', 'KP06-V', 'KP12-H', 'PB01-V', 'PB09-H', 'PB10-H'];
const sizeChart = products
  .filter(product => product.slug === 'kraft-paper-bags' || product.slug === 'paper-gift-bags')
  .flatMap(product => product.sizes
    .filter(([model]) => sizeChartModels.includes(model))
    .map(([model, dimensions]) => ({ model, dimensions, name: product.name, slug: product.slug })));
const path = "/guides/custom-paper-bag-size-handles-printing/";
const title = "Choosing Custom Paper Bags: Size, Handles and Printing";
const schema = { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "Article", headline: title, author: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Welltroy" }, publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Welltroy" }, mainEntityOfPage: `${site.origin}${path}`, datePublished: "2026-10-20", dateModified: "2026-11-24" };
const breadcrumbs = { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "BreadcrumbList", itemListElement: [{ "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: site.origin }, { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Buying Guide", item: `${site.origin}/guides/` }, { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "Custom paper bag size, handles and printing", item: `${site.origin}${path}` }] };
---
<Layout title={`${title} | Welltroy`} description="Choose a custom retail paper bag by checking packed-item dimensions, usable opening, handle strength and artwork on the exact paper. Compare real Welltroy catalogue examples before requesting samples." canonicalPath={path} schemas={[schema, breadcrumbs]}>
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/guides/">Buying Guide</a> / Custom paper bags</div><p class="eyebrow">Retail paper bag buying guide</p><h1>{title}</h1><p class="lead">Measure the item as the customer will carry it, including its box. Shortlist a vertical or horizontal bag with room to insert it, then confirm the usable opening and base with a physical sample. Specify the packed weight and carrying use before choosing a handle or paper weight. Approve printing on the actual paper and finish, not from a screen image alone.</p><nav class="anchor-links" aria-label="In this guide"><a href="#size">Size</a><a href="#example">Example</a><a href="#handles">Handles</a><a href="#printing">Printing</a><a href="#quote">Quote brief</a></nav></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container article-layout"><article class="article-main"><p class="muted">By <a href="/about/">Welltroy</a> · Updated <time datetime="2026-11-24">24 November 2026</time></p>
    <h2 id="size">Choose the Format and Usable Size</h2>
    <p>Record the packed product's width, depth and height, including any retail box, tissue or insert. Decide whether it should sit upright or sideways. A catalogue dimension is a shortlist, not proof that the item will pass through the opening or sit flat on the base. Ask the supplier to confirm the measurement order, usable opening, base depth and handle clearance for the selected model.</p>
    <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Paper bag sizing decisions"><table><thead><tr><th>Check</th><th>Why it matters</th><th>What to verify</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td>Vertical or horizontal format</td><td>Changes the orientation of the item and available front panel</td><td>Insert the actual packed item in the proposed orientation</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Width and opening</td><td>Seams, folds and paper stiffness can reduce usable space</td><td>Request the usable opening measurement</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Base depth</td><td>A box may fit through the top but not rest flat</td><td>Check the formed base with a sample</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Height and handles</td><td>Overfilled bags may not close or carry comfortably</td><td>Check the item below the handle area</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <h3>Paper Bag Size Chart: Catalogue Examples</h3>
    <p>Use these six examples to compare vertical and horizontal bags. Dimensions are shown in the order printed in the catalogue. Confirm the measurement order, usable opening and formed base with the supplier before choosing a size.</p>
    <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Paper bag catalogue size chart">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Model and orientation</th><th scope="col">Listed dimensions</th><th scope="col">Product range</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {sizeChart.map(row => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{row.model} · {row.model.endsWith('-V') ? 'Vertical' : 'Horizontal'}</th>
              <td>{row.dimensions}</td>
              <td><a href={`/products/${row.slug}/`}>{row.name}</a></td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <h2 id="example">Worked Example: A Boxed Retail Gift</h2>
    <p>Suppose a boxed gift measures 22 × 8 × 20 cm. The <a href="/products/kraft-paper-bags/">Kraft Paper Bags</a> catalogue lists KP06-V at 25 × 13 × 32 cm and KP12-H at 30 × 10 × 25 cm. These are two formats to ask about, not confirmed fits: the catalogue page does not establish usable inner dimensions or a measurement order for every model. If the supplier confirms width × depth × height, the horizontal option has less nominal depth clearance. Test both with the real box, including any tissue, before ordering.</p>
    <p>For a colored presentation bag, compare the <a href="/products/paper-gift-bags/">Paper &amp; Gift Bags</a> range separately. Its PB09-H catalogue entry is 32 × 11 × 27 cm, but color, paper, handles and usable measurements need their own specification. Do not assume the kraft and gift-bag models share a construction just because their listed dimensions are similar.</p>
    <h2 id="handles">Compare Paper Bag Handle Types</h2>
    <p>Common handle formats include twisted paper, flat paper, rope or ribbon loops, and die-cut grips. Use these examples to shortlist a format, then confirm availability and attachment for the exact bag size and paper. Check the full bag with the actual load before approving the sample.</p>
    <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Paper bag handle types and sample checks">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Handle type</th><th scope="col">What to specify</th><th scope="col">What to check on the loaded sample</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">Twisted paper</th><td>Loop size, paper color and how the ends attach to the bag.</td><td>Grip clearance and any movement where the loops meet the bag.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Flat paper</th><td>Strip width, handle opening and inside or outside attachment.</td><td>How the strip sits in the hand and whether the edges lift near the attachment.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Rope or ribbon</th><td>Material, color, loop length, attachment and reinforcement around any holes.</td><td>Grip comfort, movement at the fixing points and the appearance of the rim under load.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Die-cut grip</th><td>Cutout dimensions and location, and any reinforcement around the grip.</td><td>Finger clearance with the item in place and the condition of the cut edge after carrying.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>Send the maximum packed weight, how long customers will carry the bag, and whether the contents have sharp corners or a rigid box. Ask which handle material, attachment method, paper weight and reinforcement can be supplied for the chosen size. Request a loaded sample and check the handle attachment, rim, base and comfort during realistic carrying. A photograph of a handle does not establish a safe load rating.</p>
    <div class="guide-callout">
      <h3>Record the Loaded Sample</h3>
      <p>Keep the packed dimensions, measured weight and carry conditions with the sample reference. Record what happened at the handle attachments, rim and base so a revised sample can be checked on the same basis.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/downloads/retail-paper-bag-loaded-sample.txt" download>Download the loaded sample record (TXT) ↓</a>
    </div>
    <h2 id="printing">Paper Bag Print File Requirements</h2>
    <p>For the first review, send the editable logo if available, a visual preview, and the target print size and position. Include the bag model or dimensions, paper color, finish and quantity per artwork version.</p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Send the artwork and preview.</strong> An AI file or editable vector PDF gives the print team artwork to scale. A PDF, PNG or JPG preview can show the intended placement. The enquiry form accepts AI, PDF and PSD files for review. If you have only an EPS file, see the <a href="/guides/logo-artwork-checklist/#submit-artwork">artwork submission options</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Mark the bag panels.</strong> Label front and back, show the intended logo size and orientation, and identify any side-gusset or base printing. Ask for the dieline for the selected bag and confirm the safe area, bleed and clearance from folds and handle attachments.</li>
      <li><strong>Keep the colors and version together.</strong> Identify the artwork revision, brand color references, fonts and linked images. On natural kraft or colored paper, ask how light artwork and small text will appear on the chosen stock.</li>
      <li><strong>Approve the proof against the bag specification.</strong> Check the artwork version, spelling, placement and panel orientation. If color or detail is critical, ask for a physical print sample on the proposed paper and finish.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Use the <a href="/guides/logo-artwork-checklist/">logo artwork checklist</a> to prepare the source files and proof questions before production.</p>
<h2 id="buyer-project">Apply the Specification to Your Retail or Event Project</h2>
    <p>For an everyday shop bag, compare the common purchase combinations and decide which sizes the store should keep. For a dated event, add venue allocation, gift assembly and a named approval owner to the same specification. The <a href="/industries/retail-event-paper-bags/">retail and event paper bag project plan</a> connects these decisions to a loaded-sample checklist and a copyable enquiry brief.</p>
    <p>A natural kraft and a colored gift bag can be alternatives for the same boxed item. Request the actual paper, handle and finish for both instead of assuming either product name guarantees a particular price or strength.</p>
    <h2 id="quote">What to Send for a Comparable Quote</h2>
    <p>Share the item and packed dimensions, weight, target bag model or format, quantity per size and design, delivery destination, artwork and preferred color or finish. Ask for confirmed usable dimensions, paper and handle specifications, reinforcement, print method, sample arrangements and lead time. Compare quotations against the same load and presentation requirements rather than catalogue dimensions alone.</p>
    <div class="button-row">
      <a class="button" href="/quote/?product=kraft-paper-bags#quote-form" data-quote-placement="content">Request a Kraft Paper Bag Quote</a>
      <a class="button button-secondary" href="/quote/?product=paper-gift-bags#quote-form" data-quote-placement="content">Request a Paper Gift Bag Quote</a>
    </div>
    <p><a class="text-link" href="/quote/?product=multiple-products#quote-form">Compare both paper bag options in one enquiry →</a></p>
  </article><aside class="side-card"><p class="eyebrow">Compare actual formats</p><h2>Related Products</h2><div class="guide-options">
    <a href="/products/kraft-paper-bags/"><strong>Kraft Paper Bags</strong><span>17 vertical and horizontal catalogue entries</span></a>
    <a href="/products/paper-gift-bags/"><strong>Paper &amp; Gift Bags</strong><span>Colored presentation options to specify</span></a>
  </div><a class="text-link" href="/guides/logo-artwork-checklist/">Prepare your logo artwork →</a></aside></div></section>
</Layout>
